From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Show apps the inner screen's refresh rates

Display.getSupportedModes() filters internal displays through RefreshRateConfig,
which here only knows the cover's 60 Hz, so apps on the inner panel saw a
60 Hz display. Chrome-based apps (TestUFO measured 59 fps) then rendered at
60 while the panel ran at 120. The inner panel only shows for "Mirroring high
refresh rate", so return all of its modes unfiltered.

diff --git a/smali_classes4/android/view/Display.smali b/smali_classes4/android/view/Display.smali
--- a/smali_classes4/android/view/Display.smali
+++ b/smali_classes4/android/view/Display.smali
@@ -466,6 +466,37 @@
     return-object v0
 
     :cond_0
+    # Onigiri: RefreshRateConfig only knows the cover's 60 Hz. The inner panel (port 131) only
+    # shows for "Mirroring high refresh rate", so apps see all of its modes, up to 120 Hz.
+    iget-object v0, p0, Landroid/view/Display;->mDisplayInfo:Landroid/view/DisplayInfo;
+
+    iget-object v0, v0, Landroid/view/DisplayInfo;->address:Landroid/view/DisplayAddress;
+
+    instance-of v2, v0, Landroid/view/DisplayAddress$Physical;
+
+    if-eqz v2, :onigiri_filter_modes
+
+    check-cast v0, Landroid/view/DisplayAddress$Physical;
+
+    invoke-virtual {v0}, Landroid/view/DisplayAddress$Physical;->getPort()I
+
+    move-result v0
+
+    const/16 v2, 0x83
+
+    if-ne v0, v2, :onigiri_filter_modes
+
+    array-length v0, p1
+
+    invoke-static {p1, v0}, Ljava/util/Arrays;->copyOf([Ljava/lang/Object;I)[Ljava/lang/Object;
+
+    move-result-object v0
+
+    check-cast v0, [Landroid/view/Display$Mode;
+
+    return-object v0
+
+    :onigiri_filter_modes
     invoke-static {}, Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/display/RefreshRateConfig;->getInstance()Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/display/RefreshRateConfig;
 
     move-result-object v0
